# Anything that could carry personal data out of a working copy.
# The app writes its cache to the OS app-data directory, not here, but a
# working copy accumulates exports — and every one of them contains wallet
# addresses, balances and cost basis.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
Holdings-*.csv
Holdings-*.pdf
Form-8949*.csv
Form-8949*.pdf
Schedule-D*.pdf
Disposal-Destinations-*.csv
Wallet-Activity-*.csv
Wallet-Config-*.csv
Basis-Ledger-*.csv
Gift-Log-*.csv
Lost-Wallet-Basis-Report-*.csv
Exchange-Cost-Basis-Handoff-*.csv
Income-Report-*.csv
All-Transactions-*.csv
Koinly-Import-*.csv
CoinLedger-Import-*.csv
# Market data only — no personal data in this one, but it is still an export
# that lands in the working copy and has no business being committed.
Price-History-*.pdf
# The "not on Form 8949" companion list. Addresses, amounts, tx hashes.
Unvalued-Transactions-*.csv
# The treatment before/after. No addresses, but it is a personal tax figure.
AMM-Treatment-Comparison-*.csv
# The preparer memo and the position defense. No addresses, but they are
# personal tax documents. The generators are committed; the output is not.
AMM-Treatment-Memo*.pdf
AMM-Treatment-A-Defense*.pdf
# verify-xrpl.js --amm --out. Addresses, amounts, transaction hashes.
amm-*.csv
amm.csv
# verify-xrpl.js --out. Full of addresses and amounts.
XRPL-Verification-*.csv
